/E (The Cache-Aside Pattern improves performance by checking the cache before querying the database. On a cache hit, data is used directly; on a cache miss, data is fetched from the database, stored in the cache, and then returned. This approach reduces database load, speeds up access to frequently used data, and enhances scalability.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
